-- Batteries moved into the component catalogue (20261002000001 and the
-- carry-over script). The admin catalogue item's last structural task done.
--
-- Keep in sync with supabase/seed.sql (CI enforces this).

update public.roadmap_items
  set status = 'in_test',
      dev_percent_complete = 90,
      description = 'Session 2 of the component-catalogue work, planned 2026-09-30. The scraper now fills component_models, component_listings, panel_specs and inverter_specs, and NOTHING can be published until an admin verifies a spec row against the manufacturer datasheet -- the database refuses it. So this screen is the only way the new catalogue reaches anyone. ONE CATALOGUE, NOT ONE PAGE PER CATEGORY: /admin/catalog lists every model across panels and inverters (batteries once they move in), filterable by category, brand, published state, spec state (verified / CEC candidate / no electricals) and held prices, searchable by brand, model and part number, sortable by price and $/W. Pallet listings show a per-panel price. MODEL PAGE: photo, every listing with its retailer, pack size, minimum order and dated price; the spec row side by side with its CEC row and the spec-sheet link; a VERIFY form that records the datasheet figures and runs panel-review.ts / inverter-review.ts before setting verified_at; then Publish. Accept or discard a held price. HIDE, DON''T DELETE: deleting a scraped row lets next week''s run re-insert it -- the battery duplicate problem -- so rejecting needs a hidden state the scraper respects. MERGE two models that turned out to be one product (a listing whose part number differed from its sibling''s). ALSO: move battery_models into the catalogue as a third category, retiring /admin/batteries into it; seed the four hand-verified PANEL_PRESETS and INVERTER_PRESETS rows as datasheet-verified models so the calculators have something published on day one. SHIPPED 2026-09-30 as /admin/catalog and /admin/catalog/[id] (migration 20260930000003). LIST: every panel and inverter with status tabs in work order -- ready to publish, CEC candidates, no specs yet, published, hidden -- search by brand, model or part number, cheapest CURRENT price per unit (a pallet divided by its pack size; a price past the 45-day expiry cannot win) and $/W for panels, and a banner when a price is held. MODEL PAGE: every listing with pack size, minimum order, dated price and per-unit price; held prices accepted (dated to when the scraper saw them, not the click) or discarded; the verify form; Publish, Unpublish, Hide with a reason, Un-verify; and merge-into-another-model, which moves listings and deletes the duplicate -- safe against the weekly scrape because listings are matched by the shop''s product id. THE VERIFY FORM IS DELIBERATELY NOT PRE-FILLED WITH CEC ELECTRICALS: a form that opens full of CEC numbers is one click from "verified" meaning "CEC", the exact substitution the gate refuses. The CEC row sits beside it as reference only, and once verified the page lists where the datasheet and CEC disagree. The datasheet URL is required and becomes the model''s citation. The same physics checks that guard the presets run first; a fail blocks the save, a warn is shown and allowed. DATABASE: is_hidden with a CHECK that hidden is never published, and a trigger that refuses un-verifying or deleting the specs of a live model -- the gate now closes from both sides. SEEDED: the four hand-verified presets (SG550WM, SPH8048P, SPH10048P, EG4 6000XP) as verified and UNPUBLISHED; the 6000XP attached to its scraped Signature Solar model. The three Sun Gold Power products have no shop listing yet. NOT DONE: moving battery_models in as a third category, deliberately separate because those rows are live on /calculators/battery. Rendering could not be checked by Claude (no admin session); queries, build and the signed-out redirect were. BATTERIES MOVED IN 2026-10-02 (migration 20261002000001, scripts/migrate-batteries-to-catalogue.ts). A battery category with typed battery_specs under the same publish gate. The five battery scrapers keep their parsing and hand-verified mappings and now write through the catalogue writer (src/lib/battery-catalog.ts): EG4 and Victron pages become manufacturer-only models with no listing, Sun Gold Power lists on its own page, Signature Solar and A1 SolarStore add reseller listings keyed on the SKU. THE CARRY-OVER replayed every battery_models row through that same writer, so listing ids match what the weekly scrape looks for, and marked the 26 rows approved under /admin/batteries verified and published: 26 batteries, 11 listings, original price dates kept (a re-run had re-dated them as freshly confirmed; fixed, verified row by row). The duplicate #36 folded into #5 by SKU. /calculators/battery reads the catalogue and shows the same 13 batteries at 48 V it showed before. WHAT CHANGED IN BEHAVIOUR: a published battery''s price now updates in place and only a >30% move is held, instead of every change becoming a proposal; a page that disagrees with verified specs is flagged "source changed" on the model (spec_disagreement) rather than proposed, and re-verifying clears it. Battery verify forms pre-fill from the manufacturer page (capacity, not protection) and run the battery-review.ts checks. /admin/batteries redirects; battery_models and battery_model_revisions are frozen as the rollback, to be dropped once a week of scheduled runs has passed.'
  where title = 'Admin: component catalogue — browse, verify, publish';
